(4285475, 618752, 15207, '<td valign="top">What a shame. This looks like a well-executed exposure and the reflections are beautiful. However, unfortunately, it is very blurry. If your shutter speed was under 1/60 of a second you may have hand-shake in which case it''s best to put your camera on a tripod. On the other hand, if you did have it on a tripod but the boat moved, I''d suggest increasing shutter speed to at least 1/125 to freeze the action and dial up the aperture accordingly.</td>', 'What a shame. This looks like a well-executed exposure and the reflections are beautiful. However, unfortunately, it is very blurry. If your shutter speed was under 1/60 of a second you may have hand-shake in which case it''s best to put your camera on a tripod. On the other hand, if you did have it on a tripod but the boat moved, I''d suggest increasing shutter speed to at least 1/125 to freeze the action and dial up the aperture accordingly.', '2007-12-03 11:40:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285482, 618716, 57421, '<td valign="top">nice costume, colors, composition.</td>', 'nice costume, colors, composition.', '2007-12-03 11:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285484, 619165, 57421, '<td valign="top">very nice portrait and snowy make-up. The blue eyes (real?) are also a nice match with the background. I would have just maybe preferred a slightly lower crop overall, and the teeth seems odd, probably just an effect due to the lips.</td>', 'very nice portrait and snowy make-up. The blue eyes (real?) are also a nice match with the background. I would have just maybe preferred a slightly lower crop overall, and the teeth seems odd, probably just an effect due to the lips.', '2007-12-03 11:43:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285485, 618716, 15207, '<td valign="top">I think you have a winner here! One thing just for future... ther''es a rule of thumb that you should cut off subjects just above joints. If you''re going to show below the knees then you ahve to show the feet. If you''re going to show below the elbow then you have to show to the ends of the fingers. If you''re going to crop a person, crop at the shoulders, hips, etc. I do find I''m looking for the feet - the opposite crop would be just below the hips to make it work. 9</td>', 'I think you have a winner here! One thing just for future... ther''es a rule of thumb that you should cut off subjects just above joints. If you''re going to show below the knees then you ahve to show the feet. If you''re going to show below the elbow then you have to show to the ends of the fingers. If you''re going to crop a person, crop at the shoulders, hips, etc. I do find I''m looking for the feet - the opposite crop would be just below the hips to make it work. 9', '2007-12-03 11:44:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285488, 618614, 57421, '<td valign="top">nice one. definitely fairy tale-ish.</td>', 'nice one. definitely fairy tale-ish.', '2007-12-03 11:44:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285495, 618436, 57421, '<td valign="top">sorry, but that''s a terribly bad photo. Among other: no clear subject, harsh lighting, terribly noisy, but yet with lots of noise reduction artifacts, bad colors, lots of uninteresting/annoying subjects, red eyes (that are not read in this case) etc.</td>', 'sorry, but that''s a terribly bad photo. Among other: no clear subject, harsh lighting, terribly noisy, but yet with lots of noise reduction artifacts, bad colors, lots of uninteresting/annoying subjects, red eyes (that are not read in this case) etc.', '2007-12-03 11:47:53.000000', NULL, 1),
