(4285858, 618318, 22301, '<td valign="top">that is some excellent DoF control! also like the PP to get the overall tone of the image. I would try and get your file size larger, yours is only 93 kb and you can use up to 150 kb. If you use PS, you can look at this <a href="//dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tutorial</a> or look in your software for a Save for Web type of Save function. It will help with fine details and give smooth even OOF areas. A stellar photo, I like it</td>', 'that is some excellent DoF control! also like the PP to get the overall tone of the image. I would try and get your file size larger, yours is only 93 kb and you can use up to 150 kb. If you use PS, you can look at this tutorial or look in your software for a Save for Web type of Save function. It will help with fine details and give smooth even OOF areas. A stellar photo, I like it', '2007-12-03 14:42:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285865, 618367, 22301, '<td valign="top">I like the photo, it isn''t totally sharp but I think it works well. I am not sure if the outfit though really says fairy tale, as I think of fairy tales as from long ago and her outfit doesn''t fit. Either way a real good image though. :)</td>', 'I like the photo, it isn''t totally sharp but I think it works well. I am not sure if the outfit though really says fairy tale, as I think of fairy tales as from long ago and her outfit doesn''t fit. Either way a real good image though. :)', '2007-12-03 14:44:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285873, 618369, 22301, '<td valign="top">I like the hair and desaturation of the face. I think something in processing made the eyes and eyelashes oversharp. A trick I use to smooth skin is to duplicate the image and apply a gaussian blur to the whole layer, than erase out the parts that I don''t want blurred, than fade the opacity of that layer until I find a smooth transition. The lighting is also very smooth and fits your ice princess theme.</td>', 'I like the hair and desaturation of the face. I think something in processing made the eyes and eyelashes oversharp. A trick I use to smooth skin is to duplicate the image and apply a gaussian blur to the whole layer, than erase out the parts that I don''t want blurred, than fade the opacity of that layer until I find a smooth transition. The lighting is also very smooth and fits your ice princess theme.', '2007-12-03 14:48:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4285883, 619020, 22301, '<td valign="top">I like how you caught the dust flying in the air. I can see why you included the leafy vine in the background, but I find with it overlapping the model it cramps the composition. I may have moved the elf to the right some so there was a bit more space.</td>', 'I like how you caught the dust flying in the air. I can see why you included the leafy vine in the background, but I find with it overlapping the model it cramps the composition. I may have moved the elf to the right some so there was a bit more space.', '2007-12-03 14:52:23.000000', NULL, 1),
