(4305449, 618698, 67152, '<td valign="top">So very cool!  Congrats on the top 5.  I really love the mood on this image.</td>', 'So very cool!  Congrats on the top 5.  I really love the mood on this image.', '2007-12-10 06:01:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4305450, 618318, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AP:</b></div><hr/><i> very clever, superbly composed, and great use of DoF.  I rather like the apple looking old, makes it seem like some time has elapsed since she took the bite.  But that means shes been lying there dead for a while, maybe thats a little morbid... but i digress... really cool shot, but I think you may have turned off some voters by getting a little bit too grungy/grainy with your editing... its hard to make that work with the DPC crowd.. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The grain comes from using a 1600 ISO it was a very dull day and had to shoot indoors!! Also used AE compensation of +1 <br/> <br/>I gathered some people would notice the apple being old, but amazingly enough at least from the 1s that bothered to leave a comment, most like yourself thought it was a nice touch! hehehehe Which I''m very glad... BUT DAMN the score went down last minute... ah well I am very happy with this finish tho! 2nd PB woooooooooooooooo</td>', 'Originally posted by AP: very clever, superbly composed, and great use of DoF.  I rather like the apple looking old, makes it seem like some time has elapsed since she took the bite.  But that means shes been lying there dead for a while, maybe thats a little morbid... but i digress... really cool shot, but I think you may have turned off some voters by getting a little bit too grungy/grainy with your editing... its hard to make that work with the DPC crowd..   The grain comes from using a 1600 ISO it was a very dull day and had to shoot indoors!! Also used AE compensation of +1  I gathered some people would notice the apple being old, but amazingly enough at least from the 1s that bothered to leave a comment, most like yourself thought it was a nice touch! hehehehe Which I''m very glad... BUT DAMN the score went down last minute... ah well I am very happy with this finish tho! 2nd PB woooooooooooooooo', '2007-12-10 06:02:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4305456, 618318, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by spencerwood:</b></div><hr/><i> <b>The DOF looks a little faked</b>, there seems to be a bit of a blur halo around the apple which isn''t natural to me. The background looks nice but the apple itself is not in keeping with the rest of the image somehow. A bit too much post processing - its very high contrast, the specular highlights are burned out and the apple is very strongly colour saturated. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I REALLY had a hard time trying to figure out how you can "FAKE" dof?! hahahaha no idea, perhaps using a blur filter in photoshop? Well I can honestly say that''s how it was shot, so it''s not fake...<br/> <br/>There is a bit of a halo on the apple and that was due to feathering during the selection of the apple in photohop, I added a bit of feathering because my selection wasnt exactly SPOT on and afterwards I thought it was ok as my main focus was the poisoned apple, it''s meant to be magical so that''s why I made it much more saturated than the rest of the image... it was to my personal taste but of course no to every1s like yourself =)</td>', 'Originally posted by spencerwood: The DOF looks a little faked, there seems to be a bit of a blur halo around the apple which isn''t natural to me. The background looks nice but the apple itself is not in keeping with the rest of the image somehow. A bit too much post processing - its very high contrast, the specular highlights are burned out and the apple is very strongly colour saturated.   I REALLY had a hard time trying to figure out how you can "FAKE" dof?! hahahaha no idea, perhaps using a blur filter in photoshop? Well I can honestly say that''s how it was shot, so it''s not fake... There is a bit of a halo on the apple and that was due to feathering during the selection of the apple in photohop, I added a bit of feathering because my selection wasnt exactly SPOT on and afterwards I thought it was ok as my main focus was the poisoned apple, it''s meant to be magical so that''s why I made it much more saturated than the rest of the image... it was to my personal taste but of course no to every1s like yourself =)', '2007-12-10 06:08:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4305461, 618318, 80058, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kaarissaa:</b></div><hr/><i> this photo is fricken briliant. hopefully the scoring is high </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment! Your my fave voter by far!!!! ;p Thanks!!</td>', 'Originally posted by kaarissaa: this photo is fricken briliant. hopefully the scoring is high   Thanks for the comment! Your my fave voter by far!!!! ;p Thanks!!', '2007-12-10 06:12:33.000000', NULL, 0),
